Download Ubuntu 24.04 LTS
Setup the Virtual Machine 

CPU:       4 cores
RAM:       8 GB
Disk:      60–80 GB

Network Adapter 1 → Custom: VMnet1
Network Adapter 2 → NAT

Step 1 — Check Ubuntu version
Run:
cat /etc/os-release

We want to see:
VERSION_ID="24.04"

Step 2 — Check RAM
free -h

Ideally:
Mem:    ~7.5Gi

Step 3 — Check CPU
nproc

You want:
4

Step 4 — Check disk
df -h /

Step 5 — Check Internet
ping -c 4 8.8.8.8

Step 6 — Install Wazuh
curl -L -o wazuh-install.sh https://packages.wazuh.com/4.14/wazuh-install.sh

This explicitly tells curl:
- -L → follow redirects
- -o wazuh-install.sh → save the download as wazuh-install.sh
You should see download progress.
Then run:
ls -lh wazuh-install.sh

You should get something similar to:
-rw-r--r-- 1 ubuntu ubuntu 204K ... wazuh-install.sh

Don't run the installer yet
Once ls -lh wazuh-install.sh shows the file, stop there and send me the output.
Then we'll run:
sudo bash ./wazuh-install.sh -a

After the download, a username and password will be shown


ilestone 2 — Access the Dashboard
The installer generated an admin password. Keep that password safe because you'll need it to log in.
1. From your Windows machine
Open Chrome/Edge and enter:
https://192.168.95.134

Make sure you're using https://, not http://.
You should get the Wazuh login page.
2. Log in
Use:
Username: admin
Password: <the password shown by your installer>

You may get a certificate/security warning because Wazuh initially uses a self-signed certificate.
That's expected in a lab.



